<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#ImpactFactor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#VulnerabilityFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Vulnerability refers to the predisposition/propensity of exposed elements such as human beings, their livelihoods, and assets to be adversely affected by a natural hazard. This element contributes to and encompasses a variety of concepts and elements, including sensitivity or susceptibility to harm and/or lack of capacity to prevent, prepare, respond, cope and/or adapt (IPCC, 2021)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#medium> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#ConfidenceLevel> .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#RiskFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#ImpactChainFactor> .
